  "reasoning": "The patient presents with persistent chest pain, significant nausea, shivering, and anxiety. The combination of upper gastrointestinal distress (nausea and chest/epigastric pain) alongside pronounced anxiety and stress-induced physical reactions (shivering) is highly characteristic of peptic ulcer disease. Anxiety and stress are well-known triggers that exacerbate ulcer symptoms, and the pain frequently manifests in the chest or upper abdomen. Other potential diagnoses such as hypertension, GERD, or allergies do not typically present with this specific combination of shivering, anxiety, and nausea. Therefore, the symptom profile aligns best with peptic ulcer disease.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]peptic ulcer disease[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}
